  "items": [
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Indian airstrikes impact multiple locations in Pakistan and Pakistan-administered Kashmir, killing at least 8 people. ((Reuters)) ((India Today))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Pakistan launches retaliatory strikes into India and Indian-administered Kashmir, and claims to have destroyed five Indian fighter jets. Three civilians are killed. ((The Express Tribune)) ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Pakistani prime minister Shehbaz Sharif declares the Indian attacks to be an act of war and vows further retaliation. ((ABC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "A state of emergency is declared in Pakistan's Punjab province following the airstrikes, with all schools in the region being closed. Hospitals and emergency services are placed on high alert. ((The Express Tribune))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "According to Hamas officials, Israeli airstrikes kill at least 92 Palestinians, including women, children, and two journalists, and wound at least 86 others. ((AP))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "U.S. President Donald Trump states that there will be news regarding a ceasefire in Gaza and the release of hostages \"probably in the next 24 hours\". ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Four people are injured, at least two seriously, in a drive-by shooting at a car at the Reihan crossing in the West Bank. ((YNet)) ((Times of Israel)) ((Arutz Sheva))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "One person is injured in an attempted car ramming and stabbing in Mount Hebron in the West Bank. ((YNet))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Business and economy",
      "text": "The Walt Disney Company announces plans to open its seventh theme park in Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates, their first in the Middle East. ((BBC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "Eleven kindergarten teachers are killed in a collision between a minibus and dump truck in Purworejo Regency, Central Java, Indonesia. ((AP))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "A woman is decapitated and a security guard is critically injured in a axe mass stabbing attack by a 22-year-old Polish citizen on the campus of University of Warsaw at an auditorium in Warsaw, Poland. A day of mourning is declared. ((Reuters)) ((BBC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "One student is killed and two others are injured in a mass stabbing attack outside the entrance of Santa Ana High School in Orange County, California, United States. ((KTLA))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "The Real ID requirement takes effect at U.S. airports. ((The Guardian))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Politics and elections",
      "text": "A total of 133 cardinal electors begin the process of electing a new pope following the death of Pope Francis. ((The Guardian))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Politics and elections",
      "text": "The conclave's first ballot fails to elect a new pope. ((The Washington Post))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "One student is killed and two others are injured in a mass stabbing attack outside the entrance of Santa Ana High School in Orange County, California, United States. ((KTLA-TV))"
    }
  ],
